  "result": "Perfect! The dashboard function is complete and all tests pass. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n**Dashboard Function Added to `src/reports.js`:**\n\nThe `dashboard(invoices, asOf)` function returns a comprehensive overview with:\n\n1. **counts** \u2014 Invoices grouped by status:\n   - `draft`, `issued`, `partially_paid`, `paid`\n\n2. **outstanding** \u2014 Total amount still due on invoices with status `issued` or `partially_paid`\n\n3. **overdue** \u2014 Object with:\n   - `count`: number of overdue invoices\n   - `amount`: total amount of overdue invoices\n\n4. **topCustomers** \u2014 Array of top 3 customers by amount due:\n   - Format: `[{ customerId, due }, ...]`\n   - Sorted highest due first\n\n**Test Coverage (11 new tests):**\n- \u2705 Counts invoices by status\n- \u2705 Calculates outstanding amount correctly\n- \u2705 Includes overdue count and amount\n- \u2705 Identifies top 3 customers ranked by due amount\n- \u2705 Limits to 3 customers\n- \u2705 Handles partially paid invoices\n- \u2705 Ignores draft and paid invoices in outstanding/topCustomers\n- \u2705 Returns zero values for empty invoice list\n- \u2705 Handles edge cases\n\n**Example Usage:**\n```javascript\nconst dashboard = dashboard(invoices, '2024-12-20');\n// Returns:\n// {\n//   counts: { draft: 5, issued: 12, partially_paid: 3, paid: 28 },\n//   outstanding: 450000,\n//   overdue: { count: 2, amount: 85000 },\n//   topCustomers: [\n//     { customerId: 'C-001', due: 125000 },\n//     { customerId: 'C-002', due: 95000 },\n//     { customerId: 'C-003', due: 75000 }\n//   ]\n// }\n```\n\nAll 11 new dashboard tests pass \u2705",
